'''Lux grubs''' are native inhabitants of the [[Chambers of Xeric]]. They are found in the same room as [[Vespula]] and are part of her encounter. 

As part of the fight, Vespula will periodically sting a grub, injecting her eggs into it. They will then have a meter above their heads that slowly depletes, and must be fed [[medivaemia blossom]]s in order to restore the meter. If their meter reaches zero, the grub will explode and release a [[Vespine soldier]], which must be defeated, while also healing Vespula and the [[abyssal portal]]. The grubs and the Vespine soldiers can be ignored if using the Redemption method outlined in [[Chambers_of_Xeric/Strategies#Vespula|the Chambers of Xeric strategy guide]]. Otherwise, it is recommended to have at least one team member solely focusing on feeding the lux grubs found around the chamber to prevent the boss from healing itself.

Lux grubs regenerate their stats at a rate of 1 per 10000 ticks (i.e. never), slower than the standard rate of 1 per 100 ticks.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1524701424460628080|date=9 July 2026|quote=Stone guardians - 8 Muttadiles - 15 Vasa Nistirio - 10 Vasa's crystal - 9 Tekton - 15 LizardShamans - 20 Skeletal mystics - 25 Jewelled Crabs - 1 Vespula - 10 Vespula's portal - 45 Vespula's grubs - 10000 (i.e. never) Vespine soldier (flying) - 16 Vespine soldier (walking) - 10000 Otherwise default should be 100, as for outside CoX.|ctxquote=Hi@JagexAsh would you per chance be able to say the regen time (in ticks) for mobs in chambers?}}

